# WPFly flies 8 s at 125 m/s (1000 m) and stops: started 1000 m before HEAVY on -X it stops dead in the middle of the
# heavy cell, so the cell is wanted from 200 m out and STAYS wanted however many frames its slices take (flown through
# at 125 m/s it is wanted ~3 s and dropped half-made when the Plane leaves).
Дано select 9000002
Дано --subject selection set Translation -93750,5000,1250
# WP_Protocol's "Camera" 1003 (0,-310,0) is AutoActivateForPlayer: with no pawn it is the player's view in both Plays
# (ChooseViewTarget: an Auto Activate camera before Play from Here) and so a streaming source of its own (GatherSources:
# PlayerViewPoint) 64 m from the heavy cell, keeping it resident from the first frame. Parked 232 m south of HEAVY
# (beyond the 200 m range) at 60 m up, turned to look at it, so the frames show the cell come in.
Дано select 1003
Дано --subject selection set Translation 6250,6000,-22000
Дано --subject selection set Rotation -14,180,0
Дано run Action "Save Scene"
Дано run Scene "Build HLODs"
Дано wait-idle 2400
Дано run Panel "Open World Partition"
# Walk-up: the Plane 9000002 (Scripts/World/WPFly.lua, +X 125 m/s at 50 m, Main+Foliage - WP-SRC-ALTITUDE.scn) is the
# source that reaches the heavy cell; its route must cross HEAVY (the lead places the Plane 250 m before it on -X).
# Frame time: the editor's frame-time HUD (Stat/Profiler overlay) on during this phase - the lead switches it on.
Дано set 9000001 StreamingSourceData.Enabled false
Дано set 9000002 StreamingSourceData.Enabled true
Дано set 9000002 StreamingSourceData.ShapeOffset 0,0,0
